			"Message": "refactor(Output): Update RewriteStaticBlockSelfRef to auto-detect affected files and remove manual whitelist\n\nSigned-off-by: Nikola Hristov <Nikola@PlayForm.Cloud>",
			"SHA": "4fab2bb7a34e298cf9ea9c00697fedeedbacb2ac"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T20:48:41Z",
			"File": [
				"⠃⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				266,
				16
			],
			"Message": "feat(Output): Add HoistFunctionDeclarations and RewriteStaticBlockSelfRef transforms\n\nAdd two new build transforms to Output's ApplyPipeline that fix TDZ errors in bundled VS Code:\n\n1. HoistFunctionDeclarations: Moves top-level `function NAME(...) {...}` declarations and ESBuild helper vars (`__defProp`, `__name`, `__decorate`, `__param`) to the top of each file, before any calls. After Rollup concatenation converts function declarations to `let NAME; NAME = function(){...}`, calls before the assignment hit a TDZ. Pre-hoisting preserves the unbundled semantics.\n\n2. RewriteStaticBlockSelfRef: Rewrites class-name self-references (`ClassName.member`) inside `static {...}` blocks to `this.member`. After bundling, `class X {...}` becomes `let X; X = class{...}` so static block self-references resolve to undefined. Inside a static block, `this` IS the class.\n\nAlso update InjectNameShim to add 'unsafe-inline' to the iframe's CSP - the name shim injection invalidates the SHA256 hash. Update RewriteWorkbenchBaseURL to use a literal import string instead of runtime-computed URL, enabling Vite/Rollup to follow the module graph for bundling.\n\nThese transforms enable the bundled workbench to boot correctly after Output's tree shake + bundle pass.",
			"SHA": "3c4cbf07803c8b20cfceed4186ca2dd24682c052"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T05:26:09Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				260,
				1
			],
			"Message": "refactor(Output): Exclude StaticToDynamicImport and CSS transforms from ApplyPipeline\n\nRemove CSSStrategy (InlineCSSImport/StripCSSImport) and StaticToDynamicImport from Output's ApplyPipeline. These transforms rewrite static imports into runtime forms (`await import(...)` for JS, `_LOAD_CSS_WORKER(...)` for CSS) which suit the `/Static/Application/` path where files are individually loaded via the Worker SW.\n\nFor Output's bundled tree where Vite walks Target, we WANT static imports so Rollup can follow the module graph and emit a single hashed chunk. CSS is handled by Vite's native pipeline which extracts and hashes CSS assets into `_astro/`, with `cssCodeSplit: false` in astro.config.ts to fold every CSS module into one file.\n\nSky's `astro:build:done` hook still runs the full BuildPipeline (including these transforms) over Sky/Target/Static/Application/, so the existing path maintains its runtime-load behavior. The two output trees diverge intentionally.",
			"SHA": "5b9e387695fc9812e24274d0b447d42550613243"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-04-28T04:53:25Z",
			"File": [
				"⠀⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				260,
				1
			],
			"Message": "Merge branch 'Current' of ssh://github.com/CodeEditorLand/Output into Current",
			"SHA": "ae22fae83e8e83ac908e8af3a3159e2340b00435"
		},
		{
